1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:21,492
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June second. A powerful storm, Typhoon Number Six, is moving toward Japan. Its name is Jangmi. It is bringing heavy rain and strong winds, from the southwest all the way up toward Tokyo. Let's listen.

2
00:00:22,091 --> 00:00:24,852
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:25,551 --> 00:00:30,568
[News] 台風6号が、日本に近づいています。

4
00:00:31,268 --> 00:00:35,804
[News] この台風の名前は「チャンミー」です。

5
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:42,048
[News] 今、台風は九州の南の海にあります。

6
00:00:42,747 --> 00:00:47,884
[News] 台風は、北東へゆっくり進んでいます。

7
00:00:48,584 --> 00:00:54,200
[News] 今日の夜まで、九州や四国に近づきます。

8
00:00:54,899 --> 00:01:01,043
[News] 明日は、東京がある関東地方にも近づくでしょう。

9
00:01:01,743 --> 00:01:08,007
[News] 西日本の太平洋側では、強い雨が降っています。

10
00:01:08,707 --> 00:01:14,828
[News] 九州では、「線状降水帯」ができるかもしれません。

11
00:01:15,528 --> 00:01:22,847
[News] 線状降水帯は、同じ場所に強い雨が長く続くことです。

12
00:01:23,548 --> 00:01:28,036
[News] 風もとても強くなって、危ないです。

13
00:01:28,736 --> 00:01:35,408
[News] 気象庁は、「十分に気をつけてください」と話しています。

14
00:01:36,108 --> 00:01:42,828
[News] 川や山の近くの人は、早めに安全な場所へ行きましょう。

15
00:01:43,528 --> 00:01:45,159
[Host] Let's break it down.

16
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:51,495
[Slow] 台風6号が、日本に近づいています。

17
00:01:52,296 --> 00:01:55,248
[Host] Typhoon Number Six is approaching Japan.

18
00:01:55,847 --> 00:01:58,224
[Vocab] 台風

19
00:01:58,623 --> 00:02:06,615
[Host] It means typhoon. Japan sees several of these big tropical storms every year, mostly from summer into autumn.

20
00:02:07,215 --> 00:02:12,400
[Slow] この台風の名前は「チャンミー」です。

21
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:15,431
[Host] This typhoon's name is Jangmi.

22
00:02:16,032 --> 00:02:18,240
[Vocab] 名前

23
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:26,680
[Host] It means name. Each big typhoon in this region gets its own name from a shared list, so people can talk about it clearly.

24
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:33,159
[Slow] 台風は、北東へゆっくり進んでいます。

25
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:37,319
[Host] The typhoon is slowly moving toward the northeast.

26
00:02:37,919 --> 00:02:40,175
[Vocab] 進む

27
00:02:40,575 --> 00:02:46,984
[Host] It means to advance or move forward. Picture something pushing steadily ahead in one direction.

28
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:54,592
[Slow] 明日は、東京がある関東地方にも近づくでしょう。

29
00:02:55,391 --> 00:03:00,192
[Host] Tomorrow it will probably come close to the Kanto region, where Tokyo is.

30
00:03:00,792 --> 00:03:03,240
[Vocab] 近づく

31
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:10,336
[Host] It means to approach, to come near. The first part is the same character used for the word for near.

32
00:03:10,936 --> 00:03:18,087
[Slow] 西日本の太平洋側では、強い雨が降っています。

33
00:03:18,888 --> 00:03:23,400
[Host] On the Pacific side of western Japan, heavy rain is falling.

34
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,159
[Vocab] 強い

35
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:33,879
[Host] It means strong. Here it describes heavy rain, but you can also use it for a strong person or a strong wind.

36
00:03:34,479 --> 00:03:41,463
[Slow] 九州では、「線状降水帯」ができるかもしれません。

37
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:45,888
[Host] In Kyushu, a linear rain band might form.

38
00:03:46,487 --> 00:03:49,991
[Vocab] 線状降水帯

39
00:03:50,391 --> 00:04:00,352
[Host] It names a long, line-shaped band of rain clouds that dumps very heavy rain on the same area for hours. It often causes serious flooding.

40
00:04:00,951 --> 00:04:06,063
[Slow] 風もとても強くなって、危ないです。

41
00:04:06,864 --> 00:04:11,280
[Host] The wind is also getting very strong, and it is dangerous.

42
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:14,231
[Vocab] 危ない

43
00:04:14,632 --> 00:04:21,088
[Host] It means dangerous. A very useful safety word to recognize on signs and in warnings.

44
00:04:21,687 --> 00:04:29,319
[Slow] 気象庁は、「十分に気をつけてください」と話しています。

45
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:33,863
[Host] The weather agency is saying, please be fully careful.

46
00:04:34,463 --> 00:04:36,983
[Vocab] 気をつける

47
00:04:37,384 --> 00:04:44,608
[Host] It means to be careful, to take care. You will hear it constantly in daily life, often as a friendly goodbye.

48
00:04:45,208 --> 00:04:52,911
[Slow] 川や山の近くの人は、早めに安全な場所へ行きましょう。

49
00:04:53,711 --> 00:04:58,055
[Host] People near rivers or mountains should go to a safe place early.

50
00:04:58,656 --> 00:05:00,815
[Vocab] 安全

51
00:05:01,216 --> 00:05:06,735
[Host] It means safe or safety. The opposite of the dangerous word we just learned.

52
00:05:07,336 --> 00:05:10,336
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

53
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:13,696
[News] 今日のニュースです。

54
00:05:14,396 --> 00:05:19,411
[News] 台風6号が、日本に近づいています。

55
00:05:20,112 --> 00:05:24,648
[News] この台風の名前は「チャンミー」です。

56
00:05:25,348 --> 00:05:30,891
[News] 今、台風は九州の南の海にあります。

57
00:05:31,591 --> 00:05:36,728
[News] 台風は、北東へゆっくり進んでいます。

58
00:05:37,427 --> 00:05:43,043
[News] 今日の夜まで、九州や四国に近づきます。

59
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:49,887
[News] 明日は、東京がある関東地方にも近づくでしょう。

60
00:05:50,588 --> 00:05:56,851
[News] 西日本の太平洋側では、強い雨が降っています。

61
00:05:57,552 --> 00:06:03,672
[News] 九州では、「線状降水帯」ができるかもしれません。

62
00:06:04,372 --> 00:06:11,692
[News] 線状降水帯は、同じ場所に強い雨が長く続くことです。

63
00:06:12,391 --> 00:06:16,879
[News] 風もとても強くなって、危ないです。

64
00:06:17,579 --> 00:06:24,252
[News] 気象庁は、「十分に気をつけてください」と話しています。

65
00:06:24,951 --> 00:06:31,672
[News] 川や山の近くの人は、早めに安全な場所へ行きましょう。

66
00:06:32,372 --> 00:06:35,108
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

67
00:06:35,708 --> 00:06:41,228
[Slow] 台風6号は、今どこにありますか。

68
00:06:42,028 --> 00:06:46,444
[Host] Where is Typhoon Number Six now? It is in the sea south of Kyushu.

69
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:52,779
[Slow] 九州では、何ができるかもしれませんか。

70
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:59,124
[Host] What might form in Kyushu? A linear rain band, which brings very heavy rain.

71
00:06:59,723 --> 00:07:06,012
[Slow] 川や山の近くの人は、どうしたらいいですか。

72
00:07:06,812 --> 00:07:12,139
[Host] What should people near rivers or mountains do? Go to a safe place early.

73
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:25,124
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

74
